   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="letter">
                <div type="address">
                    <ab>
                        <address>
                            <addrLine>Maison de Famille</addrLine>
                            <addrLine>
                                <name type="geo" key="G_FRA_PARI_04">9, Rue de l’Université, 9</name>
                            </addrLine>
                            <addrLine>
                                <name type="geo" key="G_FRA_PARI">Paris (VII<hi rend="superscript">E</hi>)</name>
                            </addrLine>
                        </address>
                    </ab>
                </div> <div type="mainBody">
                    <p>Dear Miss Weaver: I got to the end of <name type="work" key="W_ULYSSES">
                            <hi rend="underline">Ithaca</hi>
                        </name> but can do no more. It contains <seg xml:id="seg1" type="note-anchor">the enclosed additional mistakes</seg>. Will you see if you can get these in if possible? Also will you please <seg xml:id="seg2" type="note-anchor">send me <hi rend="underline">La Nazione</hi>
                        </seg> as no copy was sent to me.</p>
                    <closer>
                        <salute>With kindest regards</salute>                    <salute>	sincerely yours</salute>                               	<signed>
                            <name type="person" key="joyc82">James Joyce</name>
                        </signed>
                        <dateline>
                            <date when="1922-10-01">1/x/922</date>
                        </dateline>
                    </closer>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div type="notes">
                <note xml:id="note1" target="#seg1" type="commentary">The enclosure has been separated from the letter. On 28 September, JJ wrote to Weaver that Rodker had sent the list of errata for the Egoist Press edition (BL Add. 57356-28ff.; <hi rend="italic">
                        <name type="work">JJA</name>
                    </hi> 12.203-9). This list of errors also had to be corrected. JJ did so on Rodker’s list, in black pencil for “mistakes in the setting” and red pencil to mark passages that had been marked as errors but were to stand, as they were “not misprints but beauties of my style hitherto undreamt of” (<hi rend="italic">
                        <name type="work">LI</name>
                    </hi> 187).</note>
                <note xml:id="note2" target="#seg2" type="commentary">Silvio Benco – Italian writer and friend of JJ – published a review of <name type="work" key="W_ULYSSES">Ulysses</name> titled “L’Ulisse di James Joyce” in <hi rend="italic">
                        <name type="work">La Nazione</name>
                    </hi> on 2 April 1922.</note> </div>
      </body>
